WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:00.667
♪♪

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.670
Juliette:
What if what we see is not
what’s out there?

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:04.963
♪♪

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.675
♪♪

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.676
(Metal gear locks)

00:00:09.718 --> 00:00:15.057
♪♪

00:00:15.057 --> 00:00:17.059
Bernard:
We do not know why we are here.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.685
♪♪

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.979
Bernard:
We do not know who built the
silo-

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.899
(Crowd cheers)
♪♪

00:00:23.899 --> 00:00:25.442
Bernard:
-and why we are underground.

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:28.320
♪♪

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.363
Bernard: 
We only know-

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:33.659
-the world outside our sanctuary
is death.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.369
♪♪

00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:37.996
Holston:
If you boil the pact down to one
rule-

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.333
Nernard:
-it’s do not say you want to go
outside,

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:43.001
♪♪

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:45.545
(Soldiers running)
♪♪

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:47.673
or you will go outside.

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:53.095
♪♪

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:56.181
Don’t you ever think about the
world beyond the silo?

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:57.224
♪♪

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.601
What if what we see, is not
what’s out there?

00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:01.103
♪♪

00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:02.104
Juliette:
Down in mechanical,

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:03.146
♪♪

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.732
Juliette:
there’s always someone who has a
theory about the silo,

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:06.775
♪♪

00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:08.277
and I need to find out the
truth.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.569
(Lever locks)

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:13.573
♪♪

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.952
I found something that might
hold the answers to a lot of
questions.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:18.870
Holston:
You have to stay quiet.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.832
♪♪

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:23.500
And keep your head down.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.209
(Electrical flash)

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:24.918
(Screams)

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.755
♪♪

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:32.634
Are you willing to give
everything you have for this?

00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:35.595
♪♪

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.888
(Machine hums)

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:37.681
Nernard:
The clock is running.

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:38.557
(Power-down)

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:39.766
There isn't much time left.

00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:40.809
(Alarm wails)

00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:42.144
♪♪

00:01:42.144 --> 00:01:44.271
Holston:
This is a threat to order in the
silo.

00:01:44.271 --> 00:01:45.605
Juliette:
I don’t care about order!

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.899
What about finding out the
truth?!

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:53.739
♪♪

00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:54.197
(Flames ignite)

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.782
(Screams)

00:01:55.824 --> 00:01:57.743
(Crowd yells)

00:01:59.202 --> 00:02:00.871
(Steam blows)
Bernard:
Some mysteries...

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:01.705
♪♪

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:02.706
Bernard:
they're best left

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.666
Bernard:
unsolved.

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:05.876
♪♪

00:02:05.876 --> 00:02:08.795
(Steel door opens)

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:14.760
♪♪

